  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "In 1947, during the First Dutch Military Aggression, the city of Malang
    fell under colonial control. Indonesia suffered a devastating defeat in its attempt
    to defend the region, and countless lives were lost, plunging the nation into
    deep sorrow. Yet the spirit of resistance continued to burn strongly within its
    fighters.\r\n\r\nDjaka was a young warrior\u2014determined, brave, and deeply
    devoted to the city he called home. He trained every day, practicing martial
    arts and honing his skills with firearms. Those around him recognized his abilities
    and his dedication in defending the territory during the 1947 military aggression
    carried out by Dutch forces. Djaka always stood at the front lines, whether in
    liberation operations or in desperate attempts to hold the last defensive points.
    Many soldiers fell in those battles.\r\n\r\nOne night, the colonizers launched
    a planned mass execution operation targeting Indonesian fighters. Warriors were
    killed one by one until only a handful remained. When the survivors attempted
    to defend the area against the remaining Dutch forces, they were overwhelmed
    due to their dwindling numbers\u2014until Djaka was the only fighter left alive.\r\n\r\nAt
    that moment, Djaka swore to avenge his fallen comrades and vowed to free his
    city from the cruelty of the invaders. Thus began Djaka\u2019s journey to reclaim
    the territories seized by the colonizers. Armed with nothing but the weapons
    he had, he set out alone on a dangerous mission to take back his homeland."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
